args: opentide mcp
exit: 2

━━━ stdout
Run the opentide MCP server for editors and agents

The server speaks on stdio. The editor owns the process: stop is the host closing stdin, and reload is the host spawning this command again. There is no reload or stop subcommand.

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide mcp␛[0m <COMMAND>

␛[1m␛[4mCommands:␛[0m
  ␛[1mstart␛[0m  Serve MCP on stdio until the host closes stdin

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Show this message and exit.

Examples:
  $ opentide mcp start

━━━ stderr · empty
